{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>יִשְׁגּוּ</b> Two times in the Masorah: ואם כל עדת ישראל ישגו. ישגו צאני in Ezekiel, regarding the shepherds of Israel who mislead the flock — here too it speaks of the congregation that erred through a court that erred in a ruling." "<b>מֵעֵינֵי</b> — ונעלם דבר מעיני הקהל. And the other one, in the same matter: אם מעיני העדה. ונעלם מעיני אישה. ונעלמה מעיני כל חי speaks of Torah, for it is written just before it: והחכמה מאין תמצא — so too the wisdom was hidden from the eyes of the court that erred in a ruling. ונעלם מעיני אישה — this is what they said: even if she heard from a flying bird that she was defiled, once again the waters do not test her; this is ונעלמה מעיני כל חי ומעוף השמים — for even if she heard from a bird of the sky and concealed herself as though she did not know, once again the waters do not test her."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:47.277739341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}